  "notes": "Fastned graph for the 78 kWh / 400 V NMC Polestar 2 (2020-2023), 150+ kW charger class, battery assumed near 30 C. Values are stepped (whole kW), which suggests an averaged or smoothed series. Peak about 151 kW held 9-17 %, then steps down to 60 kW at 80 %. The 2023-24 cars (155 kW rating) and the 2024 dual (still 78 kWh) are assumed to share it: Fastned dates it 2020-2023 only. Early software (2020-21) charged slower per InsideEVs and Nyland (99-133 kW peak before OTA); this is the post-update curve. Second-source check: the InsideEVs/Teslarati OTA test (150 kW to about 35 %, about 70 kW near 75-80 %) agrees in rough shape. Same graph on the Fastned XC40 78 kWh page.",
